course: dictionary
lesson: 7958
title: Recent: how new is new?
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «Recent» means happening or made not long ago. The words around it are its clues. «A recent photo» is one taken a short time ago, not one from years back. «Recent rain» means rain that fell not long before now.
explain: Ask yourself: how long ago? Time words near the word give the answer. «In recent weeks» means over the last few weeks. «In recent years» means over the last few years. «The most recent» means the newest or latest one in a list.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «Ella showed us a recent photo of her puppy» still makes sense if you read it as "a photo taken not long ago". If it still makes sense, your meaning is right.
explain: Recent does not give an exact time. A recent event could be a few weeks old or a few years old, depending on what is being talked about. Compare «recent storms» with «ancient castles»: recent is a short time ago, ancient is very long ago.
fact: Recent means happening or made not long ago.
fact: «The most recent» means the newest or latest one.
fact: «In recent years» means over the last few years.
fact: Recent is an adjective, so it has three forms: recent, more recent, most recent.
fact: Recent does not give an exact time, so use the other words in the sentence to judge how long ago it was.
exercise: «She showed us a recent photo of her new puppy.» What does recent mean here? | *Taken not long ago | Very old and faded | Hidden in a drawer | Blurry and dark
exercise: In a list of trips, «the most recent trip» is the one that happened | In the middle of the list | Never | *Last, the newest one | First, the oldest one
exercise: «In recent years the UK has had a lot of news.» Which words tell you about time? | the UK | new parties rising | *in recent years | a lot of news
test:
«There have been outbreaks in England in recent years.» What does «in recent years» mean? | Hundreds of years ago | Next year only | *Over the last few years | Only on Tuesdays
test:
Ravi says «recent» means brand new. Is he right? | Yes, it means brand new | *No, it means not long ago, which can be weeks or years | No, it means very old | Yes, but only for toys
exam:
Which phrase means the newest one in a list? | the most ancient | *the most recent | the most glum | the most luminous
